: [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"ded338b2137f704133d412ee5c98851536a97652d58142407b5113f679300ebb","event_uuid":"bc3f0163-1c3d-477e-b3aa-d8ec9fe4e36d","position":{"commit_sha":"4ad86363b37ef37a719e314cf3fbcfdf53d37902","position":"1794947878870789965-bc3f0163-1c3d-477e-b3aa-d8ec9fe4e36d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"e1dacdf2854135a75c15abe7f28cad331ef9bf9c5cb552715b74de10acbd0a36","event_uuid":"3eb6032f-be2a-4b87-9b75-3e51e32628d4","position":{"commit_sha":"7ea1407aab3be5d1d9c14f434800b5ae20676118","position":"1794948462881751937-3eb6032f-be2a-4b87-9b75-3e51e32628d4"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"1da85d232e4a8bb486bbb1c14796f4c41d6cd727cda259eb594c7618782bbe88","event_uuid":"4c768572-5ef3-4d36-9743-3658133c6884","position":{"commit_sha":"ad6f04c6b8ead6653b4284a3a71ff91362411c72","position":"1794955556787871507-4c768572-5ef3-4d36-9743-3658133c6884"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Progress: plan review certified after one BLOCK (the draft left a temporary `fetched` branch that the bare clone would copy, keeping pre-reclaim history reachable; the plan now deletes it and the harness fails if the fake remote ever holds a branch other than tickets). Claimed. Implemented test-first on branch s8dc4-dry-run, commit 8b2466a9f80: src/rebar/_commands/reclaim_dry_run.py plus tests/unit/test_reclaim_dry_run.py (4 tests: happy path, no eligible boundary, non-empty workdir, CLI exit code). lint and typecheck green. make verify is running. The real-data dry run is running in a TMPDIR workdir with GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES set; it reads origin/tickets by a fetch of its resolved commit and publishes only to a file:// fake remote inside that workdir.","timestamp":1794886487403449981},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan changed (material) after the first real-data run; a fresh plan review follows. Findings from that run, on a TMPDIR fetch of origin/tickets e7a0476397f (2026-11-16 19:34 PST), published only to a file:// fake remote:\n1. Blobless pack measured 639,372 KiB before and 105,216 KiB after (delta 534,156 KiB; after = 102.8 MiB, against the predicted 365-380 MiB). 13,208 commits in the rewritten history.\n2. The reduced state differed in authorship_ledger only, for 7,817 of 10,280 tickets: the ledger position.commit_sha values, which the reclaim re-resolves by design. Ignoring that field the state is equal. The harness's comparison was wrong; it now ignores that field.\n3. The rewritten ledger anchor was not on the branch, so enforce_since grandfathered every event. That was a pre-existing S1 defect, now filed, fixed and merged as euhedral-svelte-chimpanzee (Gerrit 3413, b45a4b7f8ef).\n4. Enforced verify-identity --all did not finish within 2 hours on either the before or the after copy (both runs hit the bound), and the after run spent its time in one full-history git log per below-checkpoint ledger position; filed as tame-melodious-veery. Advisory mode (what CI runs today) reported 49,438 signed / 874 unsigned of 50,312 events, identical before and after.\nThe harness now compares enforced verdict counts before and after instead of requiring exit 0 (real stores contain unsigned events), and also asserts enforce_since is an ancestor of the new tip. A second real-data run on the amended harness started 2026-11-17 against origin/tickets in a fresh TMPDIR workdir (GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES set, no remote, file:// publish only), bounded at 8 hours.","timestamp":1794947878870789965}],"created_at":1788046506939773619,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"18002c7d-361c-4a00-af08-6ce94a8235a2","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"bdf3-e7e3-c96f-4b9f"},{"link_uuid":"6414ac97-be54-4844-8439-c203356569f7","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"4b2a-3ae8-14ee-463a"},{"link_uuid":"b0a59d24-54f6-415e-a2b8-5e9a61510e9b","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"11aa-b3fb-f239-4f7a"},{"link_uuid":"9df9031b-6c74-4696-ad43-a8ecd04cd05b","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"5796-b469-d8a3-474e"},{"link_uuid":"4c768572-5ef3-4d36-9743-3658133c6884","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"e664-881d-c9ca-4210"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nBefore any human go/no-go on a production swap, the reclaim has to be shown end to end on a throwaway copy of the store. The epic predicts that a 30-day horizon cuts the blobless `tickets` pack to about 365–380 MiB. The CI guard last measured 648,416 KiB against a temporary 563,200 KiB budget (epic comment of 2026-09-18). This story builds the dry-run harness and produces the evidence packet that goes to the human.\n\n## Approach\n\nAdd a new module, `src/rebar/_commands/reclaim_dry_run.py`, runnable as `python -m rebar._commands.reclaim_dry_run --source <repo> --ref <rev> --workdir <empty dir> [--horizon-days N]`. Its parser comes from `rebar._cli._parser.build_argument_parser`, the same factory `src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/core/reclaim.py` uses. It chains the merged pieces and never writes to `--source`. Every repository it creates sits inside `--workdir`.\n\n1. **T0 copy.** `git init -b tickets <workdir>/t0`, so HEAD names `tickets`. Then `git fetch --no-tags <source> <commit>:refs/heads/fetched`, where `<commit>` is `--ref` resolved in the source. Then `git update-ref refs/heads/tickets refs/heads/fetched` and `git update-ref -d refs/heads/fetched`, so `tickets` is the only branch. Git refuses to fetch straight into the checked-out (unborn) `tickets`, which is why the fetch goes through a temporary ref. Fetching a revision, rather than cloning a branch, lets the real run read `origin/tickets` without touching any branch of the source. The resolved commit is T0.\n2. **Fake remote.** `git clone --bare --no-local <workdir>/t0 <workdir>/fake-remote.git` creates the throwaway stand-in for the published remote. Before the first push it is pinned with `maintenance.auto=false`, `gc.auto=0` and `receive.autogc=false`, so no detached maintenance process races the later clones, and given `uploadpack.allowFilter=true` so it can serve a blobless clone. The harness then checks that `for-each-ref refs/heads/` on the fake remote lists exactly `refs/heads/tickets` and fails otherwise, because any second branch would keep the pre-reclaim history reachable.\n3. **Shadow.** `git clone --no-local --branch tickets` of the fake remote, with its `origin` removed, the `.rebar/reclaim-shadow-clone` marker written, and `refs/remotes/origin/tickets` set to T0. That gives S1's horizon check its anchor (`_require_remote_horizon_ref`, `src/rebar/_commands/reclaim_collapse.py`).\n4. **Boundary.** The newest first-parent commit at or before `now − horizon_days`, from `git rev-list -1 --first-parent --before=<cutoff> T0`. If there is none, the harness fails with `no eligible boundary`.\n5. **Before.** On the shadow at T0, three measurements are taken:\n   - the reduced state from `reduce_shadow_tracker` (S1);\n   - the `size-pack` reported by `git count-objects -v` for `git clone --bare --filter=blob:none file://<fake-remote>`, the blobless shape the CI guard measures;\n   - the per-verdict counts (verified, unsigned, unknown-author, bad-signature, key-not-valid-at-era, in scope) printed by an enforced `python -m rebar verify-identity --all`. It runs with `REBAR_TRACKER_DIR=<shadow>`, `REBAR_IDENTITY_REQUIRE_AUTHENTICATED=1` and no `REBAR_IDENTITY_ENFORCE_SINCE`, so every event is checked and none is grandfathered.\n6. **Rewrite and publish.** `collapse_shadow_tracker(..., apply=True)` runs on the shadow's `tickets` branch, then `stamp_superseding_epoch`, then `publish_git_ref` to `file://<fake-remote>` with `expected_old_tip=T0` (`src/rebar/_commands/reclaim_publish.py`).\n7. **After.**\n   - The reduced state must equal the before state, ignoring each authorship-ledger `position.commit_sha`. The reclaim re-resolves those values onto the rewritten commits by design (ADR 0106 §4).\n   - The same enforced `verify-identity --all` must report the same per-verdict counts as before. The reclaim must not change any event's verdict. Real stores and test fixtures both contain unsigned events, so this is a comparison, not an exit-0 check.\n   - `result.enforce_since` must be an ancestor of the new tip (`git merge-base --is-ancestor`), so the re-anchored grandfather boundary is on the published branch. This guards the defect fixed by `euhedral-svelte-chimpanzee`.\n   - The only-`tickets` check from step 2 runs again, then a fresh blobless clone of the fake remote is measured. A bare clone maps only `refs/heads/*`, so the `refs/tickets-backup/*` ref the publish creates does not count.\n8. **Packet.** `<workdir>/evidence.json` records:\n   - the source and T0, the horizon, the boundary and the new tip;\n   - commit counts before and after;\n   - `pack_kib_before`, `pack_kib_after`, `delta_kib`, and the predicted 365–380 MiB band;\n   - `reducer_equal`;\n   - `identity_before` and `identity_after` (each with its exit code, verdict counts and the last part of its output), plus `identity_counts_equal`;\n   - `enforce_since_on_branch`;\n   - `source_ref_unchanged`, from re-resolving `--ref` in the source;\n   - per-step durations.\n\n   The command exits non-zero if any check fails, and writes the packet with an `error` field before it exits.\n\nThe S3 bundle adapter is covered by S2's fake-S3 tests. The `.retired` sweep (`mystical-capsizable-ibis`) is paused pending an operator decision, so it is not part of this run.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_commands/reclaim_dry_run.py` (new): the harness and the evidence packet.\n- `tests/unit/test_reclaim_dry_run.py` (new).\n\n## Testing\n\nTDD, red first, on a synthetic store under `tmp_path`. The store has CREATE and COMMENT events, a SNAPSHOT with `.retired` sources and a ledger entry the reclaim must re-resolve, and commits dated on both sides of a 30-day horizon. Its source is a normal (non-bare) repository.\n\n- Happy path: the packet records all of the following. The fake remote's `tickets` equals the reported new tip, and the fake remote has no branch other than `refs/heads/tickets`.\n  - `reducer_equal: true`;\n  - `identity_counts_equal: true`, with identical before and after counts (7 unsigned events);\n  - `enforce_since_on_branch: true`;\n  - `pack_kib_after <= pack_kib_before`;\n  - `source_ref_unchanged: true`.\n- Failure path: a source whose commits are all newer than the horizon makes the harness exit non-zero and write a packet whose `error` names \"no eligible boundary\". The source ref stays unchanged.\n- Safety: the harness refuses a `--workdir` that is not empty.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The harness runs S1 and S2 against throwaway clones and a fake remote and never writes to the source; `tests/unit/test_reclaim_dry_run.py` asserts `source_ref_unchanged`, the fake remote's new tip, and that the fake remote's only branch is `refs/heads/tickets`.\n- [ ] It asserts that an enforced `verify-identity --all` reports the same per-verdict counts before and after the rewrite, that `enforce_since` is an ancestor of the new tip, and that the reduced state is equal apart from ledger commit SHAs, as shown by the happy-path test.\n- [ ] It writes a machine-readable `evidence.json` with the before and after blobless pack sizes and the delta against the epic's prediction, as shown by the happy-path test.\n- [ ] `make verify` is run and any failure is fixed or shown environmental; the Gerrit change gets `Verified +1`; `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` and `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` exit 0.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] The harness is run once against a read-only fetch of the real `origin/tickets`, and its `evidence.json` is posted on this ticket and escalated to a human for the pre-swap go/no-go. No production swap is executed.\n  provenance: environment=developer-workstation-scratch-dir; principal=RebarBotNava; privilege_posture=narrower; instrument=simulation — the run fetches a revision of the tickets branch into a TMPDIR workdir and publishes only to a file:// fake remote inside that workdir.\n\n## Portability\n\nThe harness uses core git and local `file://` remotes only. It runs the same with or without a CI provider.\n","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/reclaim_dry_run.py","reason":"New dry-run harness chaining S1 collapse, epoch stamp and S2 git-ref publish on throwaway clones; writes evidence.json."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_reclaim_dry_run.py","reason":"RED-first happy path, no-boundary failure, and non-empty workdir refusal."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["depends_on","11aa-b3fb-f239-4f7a"],["depends_on","4b2a-3ae8-14ee-463a"],["depends_on","bdf3-e7e3-c96f-4b9f"],["parent","536b-8930-b922-4063"],["relates_to","5796-b469-d8a3-474e"],["relates_to","e664-881d-c9ca-4210"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"536b-8930-b922-4063","parent_status_uuid":"2bf7581a-a20b-4ba8-9dce-381322b291cf","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"8dc4-1541-92a7-4351","ticket_type":"story","title":"S3: dry-run reclaim harness on a throwaway shadow clone (verify-authorship + measured shrink)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["b0a59d24-54f6-415e-a2b8-5e9a61510e9b","6418cc6e-1152-44a4-bd3b-6bea87470099","7b7a49f1-dc67-4d05-aa95-4099760c8730","6062c4ff-499f-4510-a7ba-24d7f0ac170b","9f278987-3d12-4878-a8ac-4201929fc361","594286f3-0be0-40eb-ac06-db02c094d6ee","2bf7581a-a20b-4ba8-9dce-381322b291cf","69d9aea8-8b9d-44f6-82a5-28f1fb44b444","c1a7a9d4-29ac-4913-b934-f906c5317a72","9df9031b-6c74-4696-ad43-a8ecd04cd05b","2cb06545-f03e-420a-a03d-639f5a7e1feb","bc3f0163-1c3d-477e-b3aa-d8ec9fe4e36d","3eb6032f-be2a-4b87-9b75-3e51e32628d4","4c768572-5ef3-4d36-9743-3658133c6884"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1794955556787871508,"uuid":"5cb1c562-c0c6-48f1-bbe0-d351fbda769f"}